<Base title="About Sepehr"><div class="container section"><div class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">A little context</p><h1>Hi, I’m Sepehr.</h1><p class="text-xl text-ink-muted">A software engineer with 8 years of experience, currently working on banking systems in Iran.</p><h2>Reliable software. Clear thinking.</h2><p>I’m interested in how we build systems that people can depend on. Banking software makes that question especially concrete: correctness and reliability are part of the everyday work.</p><p>Here, I share notes on engineering, software architecture, web development, and artificial intelligence. Some are in English, some in Persian.</p><h2>What you’ll find here</h2><p>Technical explanations, practical examples, and room to think through trade-offs. A place to document the learning as much as the result.</p><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-8"><a class="button primary" href={href('writing/')}>Read my writing</a><a class="button" href={href('resume/')}>View résumé</a></div></div></div></Base>
